  "content": {
    "title": "Did South Carolina's Dawn Staley recruit Southern Cal's JuJu Watkins?",
    "text": "March 21, 2026, 12:00 p.m. ETCOLUMBIA — The last time JuJu Watkins was on South Carolina women's basketball's campus might have been when she took her official visit in October 2022.Watkins, the No. 1 prospect in the Class of 2024 from Los Angeles, narrowed her choice to two: Southern Cal and the Gamecocks, But on Nov. 15, 2022 she officially decided on the school less than 15 miles from where she grew up.In her first two seasons, Watkins became one of the most dominant scorers in the nation, averaging 27.1 points as a freshman, then 23.9 as a sophomore. But coming up on exactly one year ago, Watkins tore her ACL in a second-round March Madness game.She's missed her entire junior season, but her team is back in Dawn Staley territory. Southern Cal is the No. 9 seed in the Columbia Regional for the 2026 Women's NCAA Tournament. Watkins was watching her team practice in Colonial Life Arena on March 20.If the No. 1 seed Gamecocks (31-3) beat No. 16 Southern on March 21 (1 p.m. ET, ABC) and the Trojans beat No. 8 Clemson (3:30 p.m. ET, ESPN2), then it will be USC vs. USC on March 23.Dawn Staley and JuJu Watkins relationshipLast March, Staley said she sent Watkins a text after the injury.\"Really tough,\" Staley said March 27. \"JuJu is loved by all of us. JuJu is raising and lifting our game up with how she plays, with cornering the market when it comes to NIL deals. I mean, she's a business herself, and to see part of that not a part of our NCAA Tournament, something is missing. There's a big void.\"Staley and Watkins were among the investors in the 3x3 basketball league Unrivaled, which started in 2025 and just finished its second season, occurring in the WNBA offseason.\"We were fortunate enough to be one of her schools in the end,\" Staley said. \"So I've kept in touch with her and her support system.\"Shortly before Watkins' injury, the schools announced a bicoastal series with games in 2025 and 2026 called “The Real SC.\"South Carolina won 69-52 in Los Angeles on Nov. 15, its first ranked game of the season. The second will take place on Sunday, Nov. 15, 2026, at Bon Secours Wellness Arena in Greenville.Watkins gave Staley a hug before the first game in November.Did Dawn Staley recruit JuJu Watkins?In her NBC Sports docuseries called \"On the Rise: JuJu Watkins,\" that debuted in 2024, she said that her final two choices were between both the USCs.Watkins announced her commitment live on ESPN at Sierra Canyon School, the same high school where current South Carolina commit Jerzy Robinson, the No. 5 player in the 2026 class, goes to school.Staying home and creating a legacy in Los Angeles was a huge reason why she chose the Trojans.Lindsay Gottlieb has been coach of Southern Cal since 2021-22, coming after eight seasons at Cal. Watkins wasn't the only top recruit to choose Gottlieb's team over Staley's.Saniyah Hall, this year's top prospect, took an official visit to South Carolina but is going to Southern Cal.Lulu Kesin covers South Carolina athletics for The Greenville News and the USA TODAY Network. Email her at LKesin@usatodayco.com. Follow her on X@Lulukesin and Bluesky‪@bylulukesin.bsky.social‬",
